WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.411
With Mobility, models store
translated attributes,

2
00:00:04.411 --> 00:00:06.836
and editors or
translators write them.

3
00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.194
Mobility does this well,

4
00:00:09.194 --> 00:00:11.306
with eight backends and fallbacks.

5
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.155
General Translation produces the
translations through its API,

6
00:00:16.155 --> 00:00:17.675
and Mobility stores them.

7
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:23.004
Call the translate endpoint from
Ruby with a project API key.

8
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.564
Translate each new record
with a context note,

9
00:00:26.564 --> 00:00:28.595
and save the result
through Mobility.

10
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.517
Each request uses your
Glossary and Custom Prompts,

11
00:00:32.517 --> 00:00:34.641
so product names stay consistent.

12
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:38.493
Each new post now has its
Spanish version when it is saved.
